# Build an Assassin who was never a Rogue, and photograph his Uncanny Dodge.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F21. The Assassin's own
# description (lib/prestige.irh:545-548) gives Uncanny Dodge "at the same rate
# that Rogues do", on the character's rogue and assassin levels added
# together. The rogue's rate withholds a point for the first two of those
# levels (lib/classes.irh:2563, "at every level starting at 3rd"). The
# Assassin's grant used to start at 1st, which is the same arithmetic ONLY for
# a character who already holds three rogue levels -- his rogue grant has
# already withheld the two. A character who was never a rogue never withholds
# them, and runs two levels ahead of his own description.
#
# THE ORACLE is the sheet's Specials block. src/Sheet.cpp:580-582 prints the
# ability as "Improved Uncanny Dodge" when the number is 4 or more and as
# "Uncanny Dodge" below that, so the name on the sheet reads the number out.
# This character is Bard 7 / Assassin 4: his description promises 4 - 2 = 2,
# and the pre-fix module gives him 4. The word "Improved" is the whole test.
#
# WHY A BARD. The Assassin gate asks for four skills and a non-Good alignment
# and never for a rogue level (lib/prestige.irh:469-483). A bard holds three
# of the four as class skills; Poison Use is the fourth, and a human buys it
# as one of his two birth skills (lib/races.irh:197, "Skills: SK_ANY, SK_ANY"
# -> two Natural Aptitude picks, src/Create.cpp:283-289). A skill held that
# way caps at the character's own level rather than at the levels of the
# classes that carry it (src/Create.cpp:3642-3650), so it can reach the 10 the
# gate wants.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Poison Use"    # first Natural Aptitude pick: the gate skill no
                        #   bard class list carries
@choose "Spot"          # second pick; nothing reads it, but the menu must
                        #   be answered
@choose "Bard"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"       # the class refuses a Good alignment
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Fourteen ranks, two to a skill, taken down the list in the order it prints.
# The four the Assassin's gate reads come first; the other three only because
# character generation will not release a character with a rank unspent.
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
a       # Personality archetype

# A bard chooses spells as he levels, which a rogue never does. Every menu
# below must be answered or the keys after it are spent inside it.
@while "Learn which spell" a
@until "Afoot" ESC      # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
@dump:inplay
w       # wizard mode
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
@dump:switched
ESC

d                       # character sheet
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn which spell" a
@expect "Bard 7"
@dump:bard7

# The gate wants Disguise 10, Poison Use 10, Hide 7 and Move Silently 7.
# ISkillLevel (src/Create.cpp:3955) counts training and the inherent
# attribute bonus as well as ranks, so filling each to its cap clears them.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*10
ENTER y
@dump:skilled

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Assassin"
@expect "Assassin 0"            # the gate let him in

# TWO THINGS MAKE THIS LOOP LOOK ODD, and both are the game, not the script.
#
# 1. The sheet does not redraw itself. A level gained while it is on screen
#    leaves the old class line in place, so every level below leaves the
#    sheet and re-opens it, and the class line is read only from a fresh one.
# 2. The Assassin's 1st level hands over a spellbook
#    (lib/prestige.irh:609-619). The item lands in the In-the-Air slot, and
#    the game will not leave inventory mode while anything is there -- so it
#    must be stowed before any further keystroke is spent, or every key after
#    it goes into the inventory screen instead. That is the lone 's' below.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC                             # leave the sheet
s                               # stow the spellbook
ESC                             # leave the inventory
d                               # sheet again, freshly drawn
@expect "Assassin 1"

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
d
@expect "Assassin 2"

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
d
@expect "Assassin 3"

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
d
@expect "Assassin 4"
@dump:assassin4

W                       # Write Dump
a s s n b ENTER         # filename: "assnb"
ESC
@quit
